# Sanity schema conventions

- Follow `docs/CONTENT-MODEL.md` exactly. If a field is missing there, update the doc in the same commit.
- Use `defineType`, `defineField`, `defineArrayMember`. Each type has an `icon`, a `preview` with `select`/`prepare`, and editor-friendly `description`s.
- i18n: routable types (`page`, `service`, `article`, `legalPage`) have a hidden read-only `language` field (document-internationalization). Other localized fields use `internationalizedArray*` types. Never mix both on the same field.
- Validation messages are clear for non-technical editors (e.g. "Добавете алтернативен текст – описва снимката за незрящи потребители и Google."). Use warnings for SEO lengths and errors for data integrity (alt text, consent, unique slugs, reserved slugs).
- Singletons: fixed `_id`, restricted document actions, excluded from new-document menus.
- Never store secrets or personal data beyond what's published (datasets are public on the Free plan).
- Reserved future types (`priceItem`, `section.priceList`, `section.beforeAfter`, `section.googleReviews`) are registered only behind `features.*` flags.
- After any schema change: `pnpm typegen`, update seed data if needed, and check the Studio renders without warnings. Use the Sanity MCP to query the dataset and validate assumptions.
- Schema changes that rename/remove fields need a migration script (`sanity migration create`) when real content exists.
